🌐💻 Networking Commands Every Linux User Should Know! 🚀🐧

Here are some 🔥 essential networking commands that’ll make your life 10x easier:

🔍 ip a – Show IP addresses & interfaces
 🗺️ ip r – Display the routing table
 🔗 ip link – View/manage network interfaces
 ⚡ ss – Modern replacement for netstat, super fast!
 📡 netstat -tuln – See open ports & services
 📶 ping – Check connectivity to another host
 🛣️ traceroute – Track the path your packets take
 🌍 nslookup / dig – Investigate DNS records
 🏷️ hostname -I – Show your machine’s IP
 📥 curl / wget – Test APIs, download files, and more
 🧠 nmcli – TUI for managing networks via NetworkManager

💡 Pro Tip: Use the ip command — it's the newer, better alternative to ifconfig and route.
